    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6967" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">casso</span></b> , āvi, ātum,
		1, v. a.
		cassus (late Lat.). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In
			gen., <i>to bring to naught</i>, <i>destroy</i>, trop., <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 1 <i>fin.</i></span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In the Lat. of the jurists, <i>to annul</i>, <i>make null</i> or <i>void</i>, = abrogo, Cod. Th. 11, 1, 3 al.</div>
